'''Glory''' is an intangible reward obtained from the [[Fortis Colosseum]]. Players must complete [[Children of the Sun]] to gain access to the Colosseum and increase their Glory.

Every time the player completes a wave, they will earn Glory, in which the amount gained is dependent on the player's performance - damage taken, time spent, errors made, and types of handicaps selected. The player will retain Glory even if they die during a subsequent wave, but not if they teleport out.

The more Glory you have, the more permanent unlocks you have throughout all of [[Varlamore]], where citizens may reward you based on how much has been earned.  It is possible to achieve the title of Grand Champion without full completion of the Colosseum.

Glory is not attained cumulatively; instead, it works on a personal best system. For example, to unlock the bank chest inside the Colosseum, you must earn 2,000 points as your personal best of the whole run.

== Earning Glory ==
The amount of Glory a player earns in the Colosseum is based on four contributing factors: Completion Bonus, No Damage Bonus, Modifier Points, and Time Bonus.
